# 1. Purpose and Scope

This document defines the security and access control model for the OPEX Budgeting System (OBS). It establishes the authentication architecture, the capability flag model, the permission framework for cost center data access, and the data-scoping rules that govern every interaction between users and the system. All downstream specifications — functional requirements, UI specifications, and code — must conform to the model defined here.

This specification is intended to be consumed directly by development teams and AI-assisted code generation tools. All access control decisions recorded here are binding unless explicitly superseded by a versioned amendment.

## 1.1 Relationship to Other Specifications

This specification depends on and must be read alongside:

- **OBS Application Architecture Specification v3.6** — defines the authentication protocol (OIDC/OAuth 2.0 via Microsoft Entra ID), session management, API security, and audit logging architecture.

- **OBS System Context and Domain Glossary v1.11** — defines all domain terms used herein, including cost center, cost center hierarchy, cost center rollup, position, headcount plan, compensation, actuals, and Finance Reviewer.

This specification must be completed before the following documents can be authored:

- Functional Requirements: Budget Planning

- Functional Requirements: Workforce Planning

- Functional Requirements: Reporting

- Functional Requirements: Finance Approval Workflow

- UX and UI Specification (partially — navigation and screen visibility depend on capability flags)

# 2. Authentication

Authentication for the OBS is fully delegated to Microsoft Entra ID via OpenID Connect (OIDC) and OAuth 2.0. The OBS does not manage usernames, passwords, or credentials of any kind. Every user must authenticate through the corporate Entra ID SSO flow before accessing any part of the application.

Successful authentication at Entra ID is a necessary but not sufficient condition for OBS access. An Administrator must explicitly grant login permission to a user within the OBS before that user can access any OBS functionality. A valid Entra ID account alone does not confer OBS access.

## 2.1 Authentication Protocol

| **Property** | **Value** |
| --- | --- |
| Protocol | OpenID Connect (OIDC) with OAuth 2.0 |
| Identity provider | Microsoft Entra ID (corporate SSO) |
| Application registration | OBS registered as an OIDC Relying Party in Entra ID |
| MFA enforcement | Enforced at the Entra ID level — the OBS does not implement MFA independently |
| Network access | Internet-accessible — MFA enforcement at the IdP is a hard requirement |
| Unauthenticated access | Not permitted under any circumstances — explicitly out of scope |
| OBS login permission | Granted explicitly by an Administrator per user — Entra ID authentication alone is insufficient |

## 2.2 Identity Claims

On successful Entra ID authentication, the following claims are used by the OBS:

| **Claim** | **Description** | **OBS Usage** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| oid | Entra ID object ID — unique, stable identifier for the user | Primary user identifier in all OBS records and audit log entries |
| email | Corporate email address | User lookup during provisioning; display purposes |
| name | Display name | UI display and audit log |
| groups | Entra ID group membership GUIDs | Not used for OBS access control — all capability and permission assignment is performed within OBS by Administrators |

## 2.3 Login Permission and OBS User Registry

The OBS maintains its own user registry in the PostgreSQL obs schema. Every person who needs OBS access must have a record in this registry created by an Administrator. The registry record controls:

- Whether the user has permission to log in to OBS (is_active flag)

- Whether the user has Administrator capabilities (is_administrator flag)

- Whether the user has System Modeler capabilities (is_system_modeler flag)

- Whether the user has Report Developer capabilities (is_report_developer flag)

- Whether the user has Finance Reviewer capabilities (is_finance_reviewer flag)

- The user's cost center assignments and associated permission grants (stored in related tables — see Section 4)

At login, after Entra ID authenticates the user, the OBS API resolves the user's oid against the registry. If no active registry record exists, the user is denied access with an appropriate message — regardless of their Entra ID authentication status.

## 2.4 Session Management

| **Property** | **Value** |
| --- | --- |
| Access token lifetime | 60 minutes |
| Refresh token lifetime | 8 hours (one working day) |
| Access token storage | In-memory only — never in localStorage |
| Refresh token storage | httpOnly secure cookie |
| Token expiry behavior | 401 triggers silent refresh attempt; if refresh fails, redirect to Entra ID login |
| Logout | Refresh token revoked; redirect to Entra ID logout endpoint |

| **Claude Code Note — Authentication enforcement** | **Every API endpoint must validate the Entra ID access token on every request. There are no public or unauthenticated endpoints. A missing, expired, or invalid token returns HTTP 401. After token validation, the OBS user registry is checked — a valid token for a user with no active OBS registry record returns HTTP 403. Capability and permission checks follow. Never return 404 to obscure resource existence from an authenticated but unauthorized user — use 403.** |
| --- | --- |

# 3. Capability Model

The OBS uses a capability flag model rather than a single mutually exclusive role. A user's capabilities are determined by a combination of four boolean flags on their registry record and by their cost center assignments. Flags are independent and additive — a user may hold any combination of the non-Administrator flags simultaneously, in addition to having cost center assignments.

The four capability flags are:

- **is_administrator** — exclusive elevated flag. When true, the user has all system capabilities and all data access. All other flags are redundant for Administrators and are ignored.

- **is_system_modeler** — grants access to system configuration, data model management, and system maintenance functions.

- **is_report_developer** — grants access to create, modify, and publish canned report definitions.

- **is_finance_reviewer** — grants access to review, approve, and reject submitted cost center budgets within the Finance Review module, scoped to the user's assigned cost centers.

Cost center access is not a flag — it is conferred by cost center assignments and their associated permission grants, as defined in Section 4. A user with no capability flags set and no cost center assignments has no OBS access beyond a login-denied message.

| **Claude Code Note — Capability flag storage (obs.users)** | **obs.users columns relevant to capability:   is_active            BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE   is_administrator     BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE   is_system_modeler    BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE   is_report_developer  BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE   is_finance_reviewer  BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE All flags default to FALSE on record creation. An Administrator must explicitly set each flag. When is_administrator is TRUE, all other flags are stored but ignored at authorization time — the Administrator****'****s implied capabilities supersede them. Always evaluate is_administrator first; if TRUE, grant full access without reading other flags.** |
| --- | --- |

## 3.1 Administrator

A user with is_administrator = TRUE has unrestricted access to every capability and every piece of data in the OBS. The Administrator flag is exclusive in the sense that it makes all other flags and cost center grants redundant — an Administrator does not need cost center assignments to access cost center data.

| **Capability area** | **Access** |
| --- | --- |
| Login permission grant | Grant or deny OBS login permission to any Entra ID user |
| Capability flag assignment | Set is_administrator, is_system_modeler, is_report_developer, is_finance_reviewer for any user |
| Cost center assignment | Assign cost centers and permission grants to any user |
| Budget data | Read and write across all cost centers — no assignment required |
| Workforce planning data | Read and write across all cost centers — no assignment required |
| Confidential data (compensation) | Full read and write access — implicit, no explicit grant required |
| Reporting | Full access to all reports across all cost centers |
| Report definitions | Create, modify, and publish report definitions |
| Finance Review | Full access — review, approve, and reject all submitted cost center budgets across all cost centers |
| Reference data | Full read and write — fiscal calendar, account hierarchy |
| Business rules configuration | Full read and write in the PostgreSQL obs schema |
| System configuration | Full access — all system modeler capabilities included |
| Audit log | Full read access |
| Batch import monitoring | Full access — monitor, resolve errors, manually trigger |
| User provisioning | Create registry records, set is_active, assign all flags and grants |

At least one active Administrator must exist in the OBS at all times. The system must prevent the last active Administrator from being deactivated or having their is_administrator flag removed.

## 3.2 System Modeler

A user with is_system_modeler = TRUE has access to system configuration, data model management, business rules configuration, and system maintenance functions. System Modelers do not have write access to budget lines or workforce planning records for any cost center by virtue of this flag alone — such access requires cost center assignments with appropriate grants (Section 4).

| **Capability area** | **Access** |
| --- | --- |
| Login permission grant | None — Administrator only |
| Capability flag assignment | None — Administrator only |
| Cost center assignment | None — Administrator only |
| Budget data | No access by default — requires cost center assignment with standard grant |
| Workforce planning data | No access by default — requires cost center assignment with standard and confidential grants |
| Confidential data (compensation) | No access by default — requires explicit confidential grant on a cost center assignment |
| Reporting | Read access to all reports across all cost centers |
| Report definitions | Read-only — cannot create or publish (requires Report Developer flag) |
| Finance Review | No access — requires is_finance_reviewer flag or is_administrator |
| Reference data | Read-only |
| Business rules configuration | Full read and write in the PostgreSQL obs schema |
| System configuration | Full access — data model changes, system updates, maintenance |
| Audit log | Full read access |
| Batch import monitoring | Full read access — cannot manually trigger (Administrator only) |
| User provisioning | None — Administrator only |

## 3.3 Report Developer

A user with is_report_developer = TRUE has access to create, modify, and publish canned report definitions within the OBS reporting module. Report Developers can read report data across all cost centers for the purpose of building and testing report definitions. They do not have write access to budget lines or workforce planning records for any cost center by virtue of this flag alone.

| **Capability area** | **Access** |
| --- | --- |
| Login permission grant | None — Administrator only |
| Capability flag assignment | None — Administrator only |
| Cost center assignment | None — Administrator only |
| Budget data | No access by default — requires cost center assignment with standard grant |
| Workforce planning data | No access by default — requires cost center assignment with standard and confidential grants |
| Confidential data (compensation) | No access by default — requires explicit confidential grant on a cost center assignment |
| Reporting | Read access to all reports across all cost centers (for report building and testing) |
| Report definitions | Full access — create, modify, and publish canned report definitions |
| Finance Review | No access — requires is_finance_reviewer flag or is_administrator |
| Reference data | Read-only |
| Business rules configuration | Read-only |
| System configuration | None — System Modeler or Administrator only |
| Audit log | Full read access |
| Batch import monitoring | Read-only view of import job status |
| User provisioning | None — Administrator only |

## 3.4 Finance Reviewer

A user with is_finance_reviewer = TRUE has access to the Finance Review module and may review, approve, and reject submitted cost center budgets within their assigned cost center scope. The Finance Reviewer flag does not implicitly grant access to any cost center data — cost center assignments (Section 4) must be configured separately to determine which submitted budgets the Finance Reviewer can see and act on.

A Finance Reviewer requires at least ALL_READ standard grant on a cost center assignment to view submitted budget data for that cost center. The approval and rejection actions are gated on the is_finance_reviewer flag (or is_administrator), not on the standard grant level — a Finance Reviewer with ALL_READ can approve or reject regardless of whether they hold ALL_WRITE. ALL_WRITE standard grant must not be assigned to a Finance Reviewer solely for the purpose of enabling approval actions.

| **Capability area** | **Access** |
| --- | --- |
| Login permission grant | None — Administrator only |
| Capability flag assignment | None — Administrator only |
| Cost center assignment | None — Administrator only |
| Budget data | Read-only within assigned cost centers (ALL_READ standard grant minimum). No write access to budget lines by virtue of this flag alone. |
| Workforce planning data | No access by default — requires cost center assignment with standard and confidential grants |
| Confidential data (compensation) | No access by default — requires explicit confidential grant on a cost center assignment. Approval and rejection actions do not expose compensation data. |
| Reporting | Read access within assigned cost centers only — not system-wide (no flag-level report access) |
| Report definitions | None — requires is_report_developer flag or is_administrator |
| Finance Review — Approval Queue | Access to all submitted cost center budgets within assigned cost center scope |
| Finance Review — Approve action | Permitted on assigned cost centers (pending status only); mandatory approval reason required |
| Finance Review — Reject action | Permitted on assigned cost centers (pending status only); mandatory rejection reason required |
| Finance Review — Bulk Approve action | Permitted on assigned cost centers |
| Reference data | Read-only |
| Business rules configuration | None — requires is_system_modeler or is_administrator |
| System configuration | None — System Modeler or Administrator only |
| Audit log | None — requires capability flag (is_system_modeler, is_report_developer) or is_administrator |
| Batch import monitoring | None |
| User provisioning | None — Administrator only |

The Finance Reviewer capability is fully defined in Functional Requirements: Finance Approval Workflow v1.2 Sections 3 and 7.

## 3.5 Cost Center Access

Cost center access is not a capability flag. It is conferred entirely by cost center assignments and their associated permission grants, as defined in Section 4. Any user — regardless of which capability flags they hold — can be assigned cost centers by an Administrator. The grants on those assignments determine what the user can read and write within those cost centers.

A user with no capability flags and no cost center assignments has no OBS data access. A user with no capability flags but with cost center assignments can read and write data within their assigned cost centers according to their grants — this is the typical profile for a cost center owner or budget entry user. A Finance Reviewer with cost center assignments but no budget entry grants may approve submissions for those cost centers without having write access to the budget lines themselves.

## 3.6 Combined Capability Examples

The following examples illustrate how the additive model works in practice:

| **Example profile** | **is_admin** | **is_system_modeler** | **is_report_developer** | **is_finance_reviewer** | **Effective access** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Administrator | TRUE | — (ignored) | — (ignored) | — (ignored) | Full system access |
| System Modeler only | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | System config, business rules, audit log read, all report read. No cost center data. No Finance Review access. |
| Report Developer only | FALSE | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | Report definition authoring, all report read, audit log read. No cost center data. No Finance Review access. |
| Finance Reviewer only (no CC assignments) | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | TRUE | Finance Review module visible. No submitted budgets shown (no cost center scope). No other data access. |
| Finance Reviewer + cost center assignments | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | TRUE | Finance Review Approval Queue scoped to assigned cost centers. Read-only budget data per standard grant. Approve and reject actions available. |
| Finance Reviewer + cost center owner grants | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | TRUE | All Finance Reviewer access above, plus budget line read/write per ALL_WRITE standard grant on assigned cost centers. |
| System Modeler + Report Developer | FALSE | TRUE | TRUE | FALSE | All of each flag combined. No cost center data. No Finance Review access. |
| Report Developer + Finance Reviewer | FALSE | FALSE | TRUE | TRUE | Report definition authoring, all report read, audit log read, Finance Review access within assigned cost centers. |
| Cost center access only | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Read/write governed by grants on assigned cost centers only. |
| Report Developer + cost center access | FALSE | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | Report authoring + cost center read/write per grants. |
| System Modeler + cost center access | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | System config + cost center read/write per grants. |

# 4. Permission Framework — Cost Center Access

This section defines the permission framework that governs access to cost center data. These rules apply to all users, regardless of capability flags. An Administrator's cost center access is implicit and unrestricted — the grants defined here are evaluated only for non-Administrator users.

A user's access to cost center data is determined by two independent grants applied per assigned cost center:

- **Standard permission grant** — controls read and write access to budget lines and non-confidential workforce planning data (position records excluding compensation fields).

- **Confidential data grant** — controls access to compensation data within workforce planning records, including base salary, applied burden rates, derived compensation components, and total employment cost.

The two grants are fully independent. A user may have ALL_WRITE on the standard grant and ALL_NONE on the confidential grant for the same cost center — meaning they can enter budget lines but cannot see or modify compensation data.

## 4.1 Standard Permission Grant

| **Grant value** | **Read budget lines** | **Write budget lines** | **Read positions (non-confidential)** | **Write positions (non-confidential)** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ALL_WRITE | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| ALL_READ (default) | Yes | No | Yes | No |

The default standard permission grant when a cost center is first assigned to a user is ALL_READ. An Administrator must explicitly elevate the grant to ALL_WRITE.

## 4.2 Confidential Data Grant

Confidential information is defined as: base salary, applied burden rates, burden amount components, total employment cost, and any derived fields that expose compensation values on a position record.

| **Grant value** | **Read compensation data** | **Write compensation data** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ALL_WRITE | Yes | Yes |
| ALL_READ | Yes | No |
| ALL_NONE (default) | No | No |

The default confidential data grant when a cost center is first assigned to a user is ALL_NONE. An Administrator must explicitly grant ALL_READ or ALL_WRITE. A user with ALL_NONE can see that positions exist and view non-confidential attributes (job title, FTE, start and end dates) but cannot see any compensation values.

| **Claude Code Note — Confidential data field-level enforcement** | **Enforce confidential data access at the API response layer on every request — never rely on the frontend to suppress fields. When returning a position record to a user with ALL_NONE confidential grant for that cost center, strip all compensation fields (base_salary, burden_rate, burden_amount, total_compensation, and any derived fields) from the response payload. These fields must be absent from the payload entirely, not null or zero. Their absence is the signal to the frontend that the user lacks access. Write attempts against compensation fields by a user with ALL_NONE or ALL_READ confidential grant must return HTTP 403. This enforcement also applies to the Finance Review module****'****s GET /api/v1/finance-review/{review_id} budget_summary payload. Compensation fields are excluded from the budget_summary response when the Finance Reviewer has ALL_NONE confidential grant for the cost center under review. See Functional Requirements: Finance Approval Workflow v1.2 Section 9.2.** |
| --- | --- |

## 4.3 Cost Center Assignment

### 4.3.1 Individual Cost Center Assignment

An Administrator assigns a specific cost center to a user and sets the standard permission grant and confidential data grant for that cost center explicitly. This is the most precise form of assignment and always takes precedence over rollup-based assignments.

### 4.3.2 Rollup Assignment

An Administrator may assign a cost center rollup (a parent node in the cost center hierarchy) to a user. The assignment covers all cost centers that are children of that rollup node, both at the time of assignment and in the future — if new cost centers are added under the rollup, the user gains access to them automatically.

When a rollup is assigned, the Administrator sets a default standard permission grant and default confidential data grant that apply to all cost centers within the rollup. Individual cost centers within the rollup may be overridden afterward — the rollup assignment is a starting point, not a lock.

| **Assignment type** | **Scope** | **Default behavior** | **Override capability** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Individual cost center | Single cost center | Grants set explicitly at assignment | N/A — always per-cost-center |
| Rollup | All child cost centers of rollup node, including future additions | Default grants apply to all children at rollup level | Per-cost-center overrides permitted after rollup assignment |

### 4.3.3 Permission Resolution

When the API evaluates whether a user can perform an action on a cost center, the following precedence rules apply:

- If the user is_administrator = TRUE: full access granted without evaluating any grants.

- If the cost center has an explicit individual assignment for the user: the grants on that individual assignment are used — regardless of whether the cost center also falls under a rollup assignment.

- If the cost center falls under a rollup assignment for the user and has a cost-center-level override set within that rollup: the override grants are used.

- If the cost center falls under a rollup assignment for the user with no cost-center-level override: the rollup default grants are used.

- If none of the above applies: the user has no access to that cost center and the request returns HTTP 403.

| **Claude Code Note — Permission resolution implementation** | **Resolve effective grants at query construction time, not after data retrieval. Inject cost center scope into the SQL WHERE clause before executing any query. Resolution order for a non-Administrator user:   (1) Check obs.user_cost_center_grants for an individual assignment row (user_id, cost_center_id).   (2) If not found, check obs.user_rollup_grants for a covering rollup, then obs.user_rollup_overrides       for a cost-center-level override within that rollup.   (3) Apply resolved grants as predicates. Never retrieve unrestricted data and filter afterward. This resolution logic applies equally for Finance Review module API routes — the caller****'****s assigned cost center scope is injected into the WHERE clause before querying obs.finance_review_records.** |
| --- | --- |

## 4.4 Reporting Scope for Cost Center Assignments

- A user's report data is always scoped to their assigned cost centers. Rows for unassigned cost centers are excluded from query results and from Excel exports.

- Rollup summary reports aggregate only across cost centers the user is assigned to. Unassigned cost centers are not visible even as aggregated totals.

- Variance data (actuals minus budget) is visible to a user on any cost center where they have at least ALL_READ standard grant.

- Compensation data in workforce planning reports is visible only to users with at least ALL_READ confidential grant for the relevant cost center.

- Excel export respects all grants — a user cannot export data they cannot view. Compensation columns are excluded from exports for cost centers where the user has ALL_NONE confidential grant.

- System Modelers and Report Developers can read report data across all cost centers for report building and testing purposes — this is a capability-flag-level access, not governed by cost center grants.

- Finance Reviewers can read report data only within their assigned cost center scope — the is_finance_reviewer flag does not confer system-wide report access.

