# 6. Data Scoping Rules

## 6.1 General Principles

- All data access decisions are made server-side. The frontend is a rendering layer and must never be relied upon to enforce access control.

- Cost center scope is applied at query construction time — injected into WHERE clauses before execution, never filtered after retrieval.

- A user must never be able to infer the existence or content of data they do not have access to, including through error messages, record counts, or response timing.

- Write operations — creates, updates, and deletes — must validate capability flags and cost center permission grants before executing. Read access does not imply write access.

- All data mutations are recorded in the audit log regardless of who performs the mutation. See Section 8.

## 6.2 Cost Center Data Scoping

| **Flag / grant combination** | **Budget line scope** | **Position scope** | **Actuals scope** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| is_administrator = TRUE | All cost centers — read and write | All cost centers — read and write including compensation | All cost centers |
| is_finance_reviewer = TRUE (no cost center grants) | None | None | None |
| is_finance_reviewer = TRUE + ALL_READ standard grant | Assigned cost centers — read only | None by standard grant — requires confidential grant | Assigned cost centers (read-only, via Finance Review) |
| is_system_modeler or is_report_developer (no cost center grants) | None | None | None — only via reports |
| Cost center assignment — ALL_READ standard / ALL_NONE confidential | Assigned cost centers — read only | Assigned cost centers — read, non-confidential fields only | Assigned cost centers |
| Cost center assignment — ALL_WRITE standard / ALL_NONE confidential | Assigned cost centers — read and write | Assigned cost centers — read and write, non-confidential fields only | Assigned cost centers |
| Cost center assignment — ANY standard / ALL_READ confidential | Per standard grant | Per standard grant + compensation fields readable | Assigned cost centers |
| Cost center assignment — ALL_WRITE standard / ALL_WRITE confidential | Assigned cost centers — read and write | Assigned cost centers — read and write including compensation | Assigned cost centers |

## 6.3 Confidential Data Field Classification

The following fields are classified as confidential within the OBS. Access is governed by the confidential data grant for cost center assignments, and is implicit full access for Administrators.

| **Entity** | **Confidential fields** |
| --- | --- |
| Position record | base_salary, burden_rate (all applied rates), burden_amount (all components), total_compensation, new_annual_salary, salary_expense, aipeip_bonus, other_bonus |
| Headcount plan summary | Any aggregated compensation totals derived from position compensation fields |
| Workforce planning reports | Any report column that exposes or derives from position compensation fields |
| Excel export — workforce | All compensation columns in any workforce planning export |
| Finance Review — budget_summary payload | Same compensation fields as Position record above. Excluded from the GET /api/v1/finance-review/{review_id} response when the Finance Reviewer has ALL_NONE confidential grant for the cost center under review. |

# 7. User Provisioning and Lifecycle

## 7.1 Provisioning

User accounts in the OBS are created by Administrators through the system administration module. Provisioning in the OBS is separate from Entra ID account management — a user must have an active Entra ID account in the corporate directory before they can be provisioned in the OBS, but the OBS does not create or manage Entra ID accounts.

When provisioning a new user, the Administrator must:

- Locate the user's Entra ID record by email address or display name and confirm their Entra ID object ID (oid).

- Set is_active = TRUE to grant login permission.

- Set capability flags as appropriate: is_administrator, is_system_modeler, is_report_developer, is_finance_reviewer.

- For cost center access: assign one or more cost centers or cost center rollups, setting the standard permission grant and confidential data grant for each. For Finance Reviewers, ALL_READ standard grant is the minimum required to view submitted budget data.

## 7.2 Login Permission — Granting and Revoking

The is_active flag on the OBS user registry record is the sole determinant of whether a user can log in to OBS. An Administrator sets this flag at provisioning time and can revoke it at any time. Revoking login permission (is_active = FALSE) has the following effects:

- Immediately prevents the user from completing a new OBS login — even if their Entra ID account remains active.

- Invalidates the user's active OBS session at the next token validation cycle (within 60 minutes, at access token expiry).

- Does not delete any data authored by the user — all historical records, audit entries, and attributed mutations are preserved.

- Is recorded in the audit log with the acting Administrator's user ID.

User records in the OBS registry are never deleted — only deactivated via is_active = FALSE. This preserves the integrity of the audit log and historical attribution.

## 7.3 Capability Flag and Permission Grant Changes

All capability flag changes and cost center grant changes take effect at the user's next login (next access token issuance). Active sessions are not invalidated on permission changes. If immediate effect is required, the Administrator must revoke and re-grant login permission (is_active = FALSE, then TRUE), which forces a new login.

All capability and permission changes are recorded in the audit log: acting Administrator's user ID, affected user's ID, previous state, and new state.

| **Claude Code Note — User registry schema (key tables)** | **obs.users:   user_id (Entra ID oid), display_name, email, is_active,   is_administrator, is_system_modeler, is_report_developer,   is_finance_reviewer,   created_at, created_by, updated_at, updated_by obs.user_cost_center_grants:   user_id, cost_center_id,   standard_grant (ALL_WRITE │ ALL_READ),   confidential_grant (ALL_WRITE │ ALL_READ │ ALL_NONE),   granted_by, granted_at obs.user_rollup_grants:   user_id, rollup_id, default_standard_grant, default_confidential_grant,   granted_by, granted_at obs.user_rollup_overrides:   user_id, rollup_id, cost_center_id, standard_grant, confidential_grant,   set_by, set_at Grant removals are logged in the audit log before deletion. The is_finance_reviewer flag uses the same grant/revoke patterns as is_system_modeler and is_report_developer. Setting or clearing is_finance_reviewer generates a FINANCE_REVIEWER_FLAG_SET audit event (see Section 8.1).** |
| --- | --- |

# 8. Audit Logging

All data mutations and security-relevant events must be recorded in the OBS audit log stored in the PostgreSQL obs schema. The full audit record structure is defined in the Application Architecture Specification v3.6, Section 7. This section defines the access control events specific to this specification.

## 8.1 Access Control Events

| **Event type** | **Trigger** | **Key fields captured** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| USER_PROVISIONED | Administrator creates a new OBS user registry record | New user ID, initial flags, cost center grants assigned, Administrator user ID |
| LOGIN_PERMISSION_GRANTED | Administrator sets is_active = TRUE for a user | User ID, Administrator user ID |
| LOGIN_PERMISSION_REVOKED | Administrator sets is_active = FALSE for a user | User ID, Administrator user ID |
| CAPABILITY_FLAG_CHANGED | Administrator changes any capability flag (is_system_modeler, is_report_developer) for a user | User ID, flag name, previous value, new value, Administrator user ID |
| FINANCE_REVIEWER_FLAG_SET | Administrator sets or clears is_finance_reviewer for a user | target_user_id, set_by (Administrator user_id), old_value (BOOLEAN), new_value (BOOLEAN), timestamp |
| COST_CENTER_GRANT_ADDED | Administrator assigns a cost center or rollup to a user | User ID, cost center or rollup ID, standard grant, confidential grant, Administrator user ID |
| COST_CENTER_GRANT_MODIFIED | Administrator changes grants on an existing assignment | User ID, cost center or rollup ID, previous grants, new grants, Administrator user ID |
| COST_CENTER_GRANT_REMOVED | Administrator removes a cost center assignment | User ID, cost center or rollup ID, Administrator user ID |
| ROLLUP_OVERRIDE_SET | Administrator sets a per-cost-center override within a rollup | User ID, rollup ID, cost center ID, grants, Administrator user ID |
| USER_LOGIN | User successfully authenticates and loads an OBS session | User ID, active flags snapshot (all five flags), IP address, session ID |
| USER_LOGIN_DENIED | Entra ID authentication succeeded but OBS registry lookup failed or is_active = FALSE | Entra ID oid presented, IP address, denial reason |
| USER_LOGOUT | User explicitly logs out | User ID, session ID |

Note: FINANCE_REVIEWER_FLAG_SET is a distinct event type from CAPABILITY_FLAG_CHANGED to allow targeted audit queries for Finance Reviewer provisioning changes. Implementations may choose to merge these into CAPABILITY_FLAG_CHANGED with flag_name = 'is_finance_reviewer', provided the key fields captured are equivalent.

## 8.2 Audit Log Access

- Write access to the audit log is limited to the OBS service identities — the App Service managed identity (API) and the Azure Functions managed identity (ingestion pipeline). No user can write audit records directly.

- Read access within the OBS application is available to Administrators, System Modelers, and Report Developers. Users with only cost center access — including Finance Reviewers who hold no other capability flags — have no audit log access.

- Append-only enforcement on the obs.audit_log table is implemented via a BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE trigger that raises an exception, rejecting any attempted modification or deletion. Update and delete operations on audit records are not permitted.

- Audit records are retained for a minimum of 3 years, consistent with the Application Architecture Specification v3.6.

# 9. API Security Controls

## 9.1 Request Authorization Flow

Every API request must be processed in the following sequence:

- **Step 1 — Token validation:** Validate the Entra ID access token signature, expiry, audience, and issuer. Return HTTP 401 on any failure.

- **Step 2 — User resolution:** Look up the authenticated user's oid in obs.users. Return HTTP 403 if no record exists or is_active = FALSE.

- **Step 3 — Administrator check:** If is_administrator = TRUE, grant full access and proceed to execution (Step 7). Skip Steps 4–6.

- **Step 4 — Capability flag check:** Verify the user's capability flags (is_system_modeler, is_report_developer, is_finance_reviewer) permit the requested operation class. Finance Review module routes require is_finance_reviewer = TRUE or is_administrator = TRUE. Return HTTP 403 if the required flag is not set.

- **Step 5 — Cost center scope check:** For operations on cost center data, verify the user has an active assignment covering the cost center(s) involved. Return HTTP 403 if not. For Finance Review routes, verify the requested cost center falls within the Finance Reviewer's resolved scope.

- **Step 6 — Permission grant check:** Verify the user's standard grant supports the operation (ALL_WRITE required for write operations). For compensation fields, verify the confidential grant. Strip confidential fields from response payloads where ALL_NONE applies; return HTTP 403 on write attempts without sufficient grant.

- **Step 7 — Execute and log:** Execute the operation and write the audit log entry.

## 9.2 Error Response Standards

| **HTTP status** | **Meaning in OBS context** | **When to use** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 401 Unauthorized | Token missing, expired, or invalid | Step 1 failure — no valid Entra ID token |
| 403 Forbidden | Authenticated but not authorized | Steps 2–6 failure — valid token but is_active = FALSE, insufficient flags, or insufficient grants |
| 404 Not Found | Resource genuinely does not exist | Only when the resource does not exist AND the user would have access if it did. Never use 404 to obscure a resource from an unauthorized user. |

| **Claude Code Note — Authorization middleware pattern** | **Implement authorization as FastAPI middleware or dependency injection applied to every route. The authorization chain (Steps 1–7 above) must be declared once and applied consistently. Each route declares its required capability (administrator │ system_modeler │ report_developer │ finance_reviewer │ cost_center_access) and its operation type (read │ write │ admin). The middleware resolves whether the authenticated user meets those requirements before the route handler executes. Cost center scope injection (for cost-center-scoped routes) is handled in middleware — route handlers receive a pre-validated, scoped query context. Route handlers must not perform their own cost center filtering independently. For Finance Review module routes:   Required capability: finance_reviewer (or administrator).   Cost center scope: resolved from obs.user_cost_center_grants and obs.user_rollup_grants using   standard resolution order.   The approve and reject actions do not require ALL_WRITE standard grant — they require only the   is_finance_reviewer flag and cost center scope coverage.** |
| --- | --- |

# 10. Budget Entry Locking

This section records the resolved budget entry locking decisions established in Functional Requirements: Budget Planning v1.1 Section 8. All decisions below are authoritative for access control implementation.

Important: Budget entry locking is distinct from the read-only state that applies to Submitted budgets. A budget entry lock is an explicit Administrative action independent of budget submission status.

## 10.1 Lock Granularity

| **Decision: ****Lock applies at cost center + fiscal year + budget version. A budget entry lock is applied to a specific combination of cost center, fiscal year, and budget version. All expense accounts and all planning periods within that combination become read-only when locked. There is no account-group-level or planning-period-level locking.** |
| --- |

## 10.2 Lock Authority

| **Decision: ****Administrators only may lock and unlock budget entries. Only users with is_administrator = TRUE may apply or remove a budget entry lock. Users with ALL_WRITE standard grant, System Modelers, Report Developers, and Finance Reviewers may not apply or remove locks. The Administrator capability flag supersedes cost center access grants for locking operations — an Administrator may lock any cost center regardless of whether they have an explicit cost center access grant for it.** |
| --- |

## 10.3 Locked-State Permissions

| **User Type** | **Permitted Operations on a Locked Budget** |
| --- | --- |
| Administrator | Full read and write access. Budget entry locks do not restrict Administrator operations. |
| ALL_WRITE standard grant (non-Administrator) | Fully read-only. No budget line creates, updates, or deletes. No vendor line item creates, updates, or deletes. No budget workflow submission. The Save button and all editable cells are suppressed in the UI. The API returns HTTP 403 for any write attempt against a locked combination. |
| ALL_READ standard grant | Read-only — unchanged from their normal access level. |
| System Modeler / Report Developer | Read access per their normal capability. No write access to budget lines regardless of lock state. |
| Finance Reviewer | Read-only view of budget data within their assigned cost center scope (standard grant permitting). Finance Reviewers cannot submit, approve, or reject a locked budget — the submission API returns HTTP 409 for locked combinations. Finance Reviewer approve and reject actions operate on submitted budgets; a lock does not prevent approval actions on already-submitted budgets. |

## 10.4 Lock Audit Events

| **Event Type** | **Captured Fields** |
| --- | --- |
| BUDGET_LOCK_APPLIED | version_id, cost_center_id, fiscal_year, user_id (must be Administrator), timestamp |
| BUDGET_LOCK_REMOVED | version_id, cost_center_id, fiscal_year, user_id (must be Administrator), timestamp |

## 10.5 Lock Schema and API

| **Claude Code Note — Budget entry lock schema and API** | **New table: obs.budget_version_locks   lock_id        STRING NOT NULL (generated UUID)   version_id     STRING NOT NULL  -- FK obs.budget_versions   cost_center_id STRING NOT NULL   fiscal_year    INT NOT NULL   is_locked      BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE   locked_at      TIMESTAMP (nullable)   locked_by      STRING (nullable — user_id of locking Administrator)   PRIMARY KEY (version_id, cost_center_id, fiscal_year) POST /api/v1/budget-version-locks   Body: { version_id, cost_center_id, fiscal_year, action: ****'****lock****'**** │ ****'****unlock****'**** }   Authorization: is_administrator = TRUE required. Returns HTTP 403 otherwise.   Returns HTTP 200 on success. All budget line write endpoints (PUT /api/v1/budget-lines/bulk etc.) must check obs.budget_version_locks before processing. If is_locked = TRUE and caller is not Administrator:   return HTTP 403 with message ****'****Budget entry is locked for this cost center, fiscal year, and version.****'**** Write BUDGET_LOCK_APPLIED or BUDGET_LOCK_REMOVED audit event after successful state change.** |
| --- | --- |

## 10.6 Lock Display (UI)

- When a budget is locked, a lock status banner is displayed in the Budget Planning module: 'Budget entry locked — contact your Administrator to unlock.'

- A lock icon is displayed in the budget version selector alongside the version name.

- The budget entry grid renders in read-only mode for all non-Administrator users when locked — no editable cells, no Save button, no Submit button.

# 11. Acceptance Criteria

Each criterion below must be verified by automated test or documented manual test procedure before the security and access control implementation is considered complete.

## 11.1 Authentication and Login Permission

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-AUTH-01** | A request with no access token returns HTTP 401 on every API endpoint. |
| **AC-AUTH-02** | A request with an expired access token returns HTTP 401. |
| **AC-AUTH-03** | A valid Entra ID token for a user with no OBS registry record returns HTTP 403. |
| **AC-AUTH-04** | A valid Entra ID token for a user with is_active = FALSE returns HTTP 403. |
| **AC-AUTH-05** | A user whose is_active is set to FALSE cannot complete a new OBS login even while their Entra ID account remains active. |
| **AC-AUTH-06** | Refresh tokens are stored in httpOnly secure cookies and access tokens in memory only — neither is accessible via localStorage. |
| **AC-AUTH-07** | Logout revokes the refresh token and redirects to the Entra ID logout endpoint. |

## 11.2 Capability Flag Enforcement

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-CAP-01** | A user with is_administrator = TRUE can read and write budget lines and position records for any cost center without a cost center assignment. |
| **AC-CAP-02** | A user with is_administrator = TRUE has implicit full access to all compensation data without any confidential grant. |
| **AC-CAP-03** | A user with is_system_modeler = TRUE and no cost center assignments cannot read or write budget lines or position records. |
| **AC-CAP-04** | A user with is_report_developer = TRUE and no cost center assignments cannot read or write budget lines or position records. |
| **AC-CAP-05** | A user with is_system_modeler = TRUE can write business rules configuration. A user without this flag or is_administrator cannot. |
| **AC-CAP-06** | A user with is_report_developer = TRUE can create and publish report definitions. A user without this flag or is_administrator cannot. |
| **AC-CAP-07** | A user with both is_system_modeler = TRUE and is_report_developer = TRUE has all capabilities of both flags combined. |
| **AC-CAP-08** | The system prevents the last active Administrator from being deactivated or having is_administrator set to FALSE. |
| **AC-CAP-09** | A user with is_finance_reviewer = TRUE and no cost center assignments can access the Finance Review module navigation item and API routes but receives no finance review records in the Approval Queue response. |
| **AC-CAP-10** | A user without is_finance_reviewer = TRUE and without is_administrator = TRUE calling any Finance Review API endpoint receives HTTP 403, regardless of any cost center grants they hold. |
| **AC-CAP-11** | Setting or clearing the is_finance_reviewer flag generates a FINANCE_REVIEWER_FLAG_SET audit event with old_value and new_value captured. Only Administrator tokens may set or clear this flag — non-Administrator attempts return HTTP 403. |

## 11.3 Cost Center Access and Grant Enforcement

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-GRANT-01** | A user with no cost center assignments cannot read or write any budget lines or position records. |
| **AC-GRANT-02** | A user with ALL_READ standard grant on a cost center can read but not write budget lines for that cost center. |
| **AC-GRANT-03** | A user with ALL_WRITE standard grant on a cost center can read and write budget lines for that cost center. |
| **AC-GRANT-04** | A user assigned via a rollup can access all child cost centers of that rollup. |
| **AC-GRANT-05** | A new cost center added under a rollup is automatically accessible to users assigned to that rollup. |
| **AC-GRANT-06** | A per-cost-center override within a rollup assignment takes precedence over the rollup default grant for that cost center. |
| **AC-GRANT-07** | An individual cost center assignment takes precedence over any rollup-based grant for that same cost center. |
| **AC-GRANT-08** | Cost center scope is applied in the SQL WHERE clause at query construction time — verified by query plan inspection in automated tests. |

## 11.4 Confidential Data Enforcement

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-CONF-01** | A user with ALL_NONE confidential grant on a cost center receives no compensation fields in position API responses for that cost center — fields are absent from the payload, not null. |
| **AC-CONF-02** | A user with ALL_NONE confidential grant cannot write compensation data for positions in that cost center — the attempt returns HTTP 403. |
| **AC-CONF-03** | A user with ALL_READ confidential grant can read but not write compensation data for an assigned cost center. |
| **AC-CONF-04** | A System Modeler or Report Developer with no cost center assignments and no explicit confidential grant receives no compensation fields for any cost center. |
| **AC-CONF-05** | An Administrator receives full compensation data for all cost centers without any explicit grant. |
| **AC-CONF-06** | Excel export excludes compensation columns for cost centers where the exporting user has ALL_NONE confidential grant. |
| **AC-CONF-07** | A Finance Reviewer with ALL_NONE confidential grant on a cost center receives no compensation fields in the budget_summary payload of the GET /api/v1/finance-review/{review_id} response — fields are absent from the payload, not null or zero. |

## 11.5 Audit Log

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-AUDIT-01** | Every login permission grant and revocation generates an audit record with all required fields. |
| **AC-AUDIT-02** | Every capability flag change generates an audit record capturing previous and new flag state. |
| **AC-AUDIT-03** | Every cost center grant addition, modification, and removal generates an audit record. |
| **AC-AUDIT-04** | Every login and login denial generates an audit record. |
| **AC-AUDIT-05** | Audit records cannot be updated or deleted via any API endpoint or direct PostgreSQL write by any user; the BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE trigger on obs.audit_log rejects such operations. |
| **AC-AUDIT-06** | A user with only cost center access (no capability flags set) cannot read the audit log. A user with is_finance_reviewer = TRUE and no other capability flags cannot read the audit log. |
| **AC-AUDIT-07** | Audit records are retained for a minimum of 3 years as enforced by the PostgreSQL retention policy. |

## 11.6 Budget Entry Locking

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-LOCK-01** | Only Administrator tokens may call POST /api/v1/budget-version-locks. Non-Administrator calls return HTTP 403. |
| **AC-LOCK-02** | When is_locked = TRUE for a cost center + fiscal year + version, all budget line write endpoints return HTTP 403 for non-Administrator callers. |
| **AC-LOCK-03** | Administrator tokens bypass the lock check — write operations by Administrators succeed regardless of lock state. |
| **AC-LOCK-04** | Applying a lock generates a BUDGET_LOCK_APPLIED audit event with version_id, cost_center_id, fiscal_year, user_id, and timestamp. |
| **AC-LOCK-05** | Removing a lock generates a BUDGET_LOCK_REMOVED audit event with version_id, cost_center_id, fiscal_year, user_id, and timestamp. |
| **AC-LOCK-06** | The lock status banner and read-only grid are rendered in the Budget Planning module for all non-Administrator users when the selected cost center + fiscal year + version combination has is_locked = TRUE. |

